.Dd November 24, 2026
.Dt EXT2+ 5
.Os Spore
.Sh NAME
.Nm ext2+
.Nd Spore disk filesystem with a growable inode store
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Spore-built system roots use ext2+.
File data and directory entries use the ext2 layout.
A hidden store lets the filesystem allocate more inode records from free
data blocks as the number of files grows.
.Pp
The superblock marks the format with incompatibility bit
.Li 0x80000000 .
The first block of
.Pa /.spore-inodes
holds the store header.
Dynamic inode numbers start at
.Li 0x40000000 .
The allocator reuses freed slots before growing the store.
Spore-built disks grow the store in groups of 256 inode records.
.Sh FILES
.Pa /.spore-inodes
stores filesystem metadata and is hidden from root directory listings.
